{{letter|frr}}

# {{Latn-def|frr|letter}}

====Usage notes====
* In the syllable [[coda]], ⟨{{l|frr||r}}⟩ is vowelized to {{IPAchar|[ɐ̯]}}, creating diphthongs (similarly to German and non-rhotic English). After ⟨{{l|frr||ia, ua}}⟩, insofar as they have {{IPAchar|[ɐ̯]}} to begin with, it may be lost entirely.
* In Sylt and Föhr-Amrum Frisian, ⟨{{l|frr||r}}⟩ before a voiceless [[stop]] is frequently not vowelized, but becomes {{IPAchar|[x]}} instead. This development is not related (or at least not directly so) to the use of {{w|uvular R}}, since it happens equally in those speakers who say {{IPAchar|[r]}}.

